      "explanation": "Benzodiazepines are deliriogenic and should be avoided in delirium with the exception of alcohol withdrawal delirium or when used in combination with a neuroleptic for acute tranquilization. Anticholinergics should also be avoided because they worsen delirium. Antipsychotics such as quetiapine and risperidone are commonly used to manage the behavioral and psychological feature of delirium, though it bears noting that no medication is approved by the FDA for delirium. In a patient with Parkinson's disease, quetiapine is typically preferred as a first-line agent. Buspirone does not have a role in acute management of delirium.",
